Z||000003||theogre||10-25-2001||07:12 PM||||The volume control switch or shaft may be messing up. Pull out gently on the knob next time it does it. I'm not sure how fixable it is but that might tell you what's up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-25-2001||07:28 PM||||If the display remains on, won't it drain the battery?  Time to fix or replace the radio.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Butter||10-26-2001||12:50 PM||||theogre,<BR>Thanks I'll try that next time I catch it acting up.<P>Old Lar,<BR>It hasn't run my battery down yet.  I haven't stuck around long enough to see when it goes back off.  I just noticed it staying on when I turn off the car but before morning it goes out.<P>The display has suffered threw the years and is not always illuminated properly upon first coming on.  Also sometimes in heat the tuner does not work properly on the higher frequences of the FM band.  A little slap on the side usually straightens it out till its turned off again and allowed to heat back up in the interior.<BR>I have another stock stereo to replace it with but it does not have the equalizer and I'd like to keep that as long as I can.  I was mainly wondering if this was common with the stock type of stereo that's in it and if someone knew a fix for it.  I wanted to keep that part stock on the car as I kinda got attached to the stock type radios in cars since my first 63 Impala with tubes in the radio.  Seems to add a nostalgic date to any car according to the stereo it came equiped with.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000006||citybythesea||10-26-2001||01:09 PM||||Butter,<BR>I have the same problems with my radio.  i took it apart and cleaned some of the connections and it helped for a while.  Now I'm back to smacking the side to get it to tune.  My clock has the same problem. I took out the fuse that controls the memory and clock to kill the display. Now when I open and close the door the display will come on for about 10-15 sec. and then go off. Can't figure that one out. I just ordered another radio(allmost the same) to replace it with. Hope this cures the problem.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||84fieroman||10-28-2001||07:21 PM||||Butter,<P>Had similar problem with my radio.  Would not go into stereo mode and would not tune to channels on the upper end of band.  Could tap side of dash and it would correct problem for short time.  Went to junk yard and got radios out of several GM cars and all had the same problem.  After the 4th time finally found one that was O.K.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000008||Butter||10-29-2001||10:36 AM||||Thanks Yall All,<BR>The weather has turned a little colder hear and this problem has not shown up since this occured.  After looking at your responses seems this GM radio is more inclined to give problems in a warmer climate.  The spare radio I have is from north of hear and was in better shape but has no equalizer on it.  Does anyone know if the displays and such are interchangeable on those two GM radios?  They appear similar in some ways.<BR>||||reg||1
